diff -ruN -x ORIGIN.md -x ORIGIN.sha256 -x ORIGIN.diff -x __pycache__ -x .DS_Store a/README.md b/README.md
--- a/README.md	2026-11-01 07:15:15
+++ b/README.md	2026-11-01 12:43:57
@@ -6,6 +6,18 @@
 
 Linked into XNU by `unixnu build kernel`.
 
+iPadOS 27 copy (xnu-12377, arm64e): built with `NATIVE_UFS_SOURCE_API=1`, `NATIVE_VERIFIED_POLICY_HANDOFF=1` and the `Source*.cpp` from UniXNU-sheng.
+`make-source-base.py` turns the public `IOBlockStorageDevice.cpp` into the kernel's copy; `SourceStorage.cpp` loads the original IOStorageFamily and
+APFS, registers the classes and starts this driver from `bsd_init` (no IOKit personality). The root policies come from the loader
+(`/chosen/memory-map/RootPolicies`, `SourceRootPolicies.cpp`); a header-only policy reads its hash table from the data object `<window>.vroot` of a
+version 2 manifest (flags 3, 4096-byte blocks; `readPolicyTable`).
+
+Root base (`pagani-root-base-mib`, default 0, 27 uses 10240, its slot B 27648): the root image starts that far into the partition, so that a second
+system's root sits beside the first one. The manifest, the windows and the data objects hang off `rootImageFirst`, and everything below the image
+counts as taken in the log's and the store's overlap checks (`ufsLogPlan`, `ufsStorePlan`). A base outside the partition is refused and a base with no
+manifest behind it publishes nothing: it never falls back to the partition's start. Base 0 is the mainline's behaviour for a version 1 manifest.
+Tests: `tests/RootBase.cpp`, and `tests/RootBaseMainline.cpp` (`check_root_path_host.py --mainline DIR`), which compares base 0 with the mainline's headers.
+
 Solid state: `declareSolidState` (here and in NativeRamBlock, before `registerService`) sets `Medium Type` = `Solid State` in the device's
 `Device Characteristics`. `IOBlockStorageDriver::handleStart` reads it from its provider and `DKIOCISSOLIDSTATE` from the parents of the
 media, an APFS volume's too; the answer sets `MNTK_SSD` and the device's throttle table. All it changes on iOS, as read in XNU and not
